# lockstep-baseline — the version from which each nested module is REQUIRED to
# carry a tag in lockstep with the root (release-versioning.md P2).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The lockstep module set is DISCOVERED from the module
# tree (scripts/lockstep-modules.sh), but "which modules exist" does not answer
# "since when was each one required in a release". Two facts measured on this
# repository rule out inferring it:
#
#   - Auditing a discovered module over ALL history is unsatisfiable. Every root
#     tag cut before a module existed has no counterpart and published tags are
#     immutable, so no reachable state passes.
#   - Inferring the start from the commit that added the module's go.mod is
#     equally unsatisfiable here: sdk/go/gorm/conformance's go.mod landed in
#     e75810a (2026-08-13) and 27 root tags postdate it.
#
# And inferring it from the module's FIRST TAG is a fail-open: a module with no
# tags is scoped out entirely, so the release that should have cut its first tag
# is exactly the one nothing checks. Announcing that gap is not the same as
# closing it — a success exit is a success exit however it is worded.
#
# So the requirement is DECLARED, in version control, where changing it is a
# reviewable act rather than a side effect of the tree.
#
# FORMAT: "<module> <version|unreleased>", one per line, # for comments.
#
#   <version>     the module must have a counterpart for every root tag at or
#                 after this one, by git ancestry. A baseline naming a tag that
#                 does not exist yet owes nothing yet — that is how the first
#                 release including a module is cut: set the baseline to the
#                 version you are about to cut.
#   unreleased    the module is not part of any release yet. It is OUT OF SCOPE
#                 for the history audit, and `make release-alpha` REFUSES until
#                 someone decides otherwise here.
#
# A discovered module with NO line at all is an error in both: an undeclared
# module is worse than one declared unreleased, because nobody chose it.

sdk/go v0.1.0-alpha

# go-qrdb#50 ruled this a third lockstep namespace on 2026-08-20 and its go.mod
